@startuml
@startuml

salt
{
  <b>DEFINE THE CONVENTIONS FOR AN INSTRUMENT</b>  { <b>Instrument</b> | Convention | Terms | Review | Outcome }
  --
  {
    {
      <b>1. Choose the instrument</b>
      --
      {#
        Filter the families | "^swap                    "
      }
      {#
        Family | Convention entity | Conventions
        Deposit | refdata.deposit_conventions | 2
        <b>Swap</b> | refdata.swap_conventions | 3
        OIS | refdata.ois_conventions | 1
        FRA | refdata.fra_conventions | 0
        ... 21 more families ...
      }
      [ Continue ]
      <i>A family with no convention opens the terms step with an empty form.</i>
    } | {
      <b>2. Choose the convention</b>
      --
      {#
        Search EUR-6M | "^EUR-6M                  "
      }
      {#
        Convention | Modified by | Recorded at | Version | Actions
        <b>EUR-6M-SWAP-CONVENTIONS</b> | m.okafor | 2026-09-14 11:02 | v3 | [ Edit ] [ History ]
        USD-3M-SWAP-CONVENTIONS | j.smith | 2026-08-30 16:41 | v2 | [ Edit ] [ History ]
      }
      [ Back ] | [ New swap convention ]
      <i>The filter takes id_one_of only: it filters by id, not by a term.</i>
    }
  }
  --
  {
    {
      <b>3. Author its terms</b>
      --
      {#
        Convention | swap_convention
      }
      <b>Fixed leg</b>
      {#
        Field | Value | Source
        Fixed Calendar | ^TARGET^ | from calendars
        Fixed Frequency | ^Annual^ | from payment frequencies
        Fixed Convention | ^ModifiedFollowing^ | from business day conventions
        Fixed Day Count Fraction | ^30/360^ | from day count fractions
        Index | ^EUR-EURIBOR-6M^ | from floating indices
        Float Frequency | ^Semiannual^ | from payment frequencies
        Sub-Periods Coupon Type | ^Compounding^ | from sub-period coupon types
      }
      [ Edit calendars... ] | [ Back ] | [ Review ]
      <i>Every field the model carries. A term that is a pick is not edited here.</i>
      --
      <b>3b. History (the Terms step's own view)</b>
      version: { v1 | v2 | <b>v3</b> } | [ hide the diff ]
      {#
        Field | version 2 to version 3
        Fixed Frequency | Annual -> Annual
        Fixed Day Count Fraction | 30/360 -> 30/360
        Sub-Periods Coupon Type | (empty) -> Compounding
      }
      by m.okafor at 2026-09-14 11:02, with the diff against version 2
      [ Back to the terms ] | [ Close ]
      <i>The server has no draft version: history.get returns saved versions only.</i>
    } | {
      <b>4. Review</b>
      --
      {#
        Field | Value
        Fixed leg |
        Fixed Calendar | TARGET
        Fixed Frequency | Annual
        Fixed Day Count Fraction | 30/360
        Floating leg |
        Index | EUR-EURIBOR-6M
      }
      3 fields differ from the version read.
      [ ] Prototype: make the referenced lookup missing
      [ Back ] | [ Save the convention ]
      --
      <b>5. Outcome</b>
      **EUR-6M-SWAP-CONVENTIONS is saved as version 4**
      A trade that picks Swap reads these terms.
      [ See its history ] | [ Back to the list ] | [ Another instrument ]
      --
      <b>6. Refused</b>  (its own screen, no rail place)
      **The write was refused**
      swap_convention was not changed. It keeps version 3.
      {#
        Refusal | Detail
        Convention | EUR-6M-SWAP-CONVENTIONS
        Version | 3 - unchanged by this attempt
        Raised on | Author its terms
        Refusal kind | a term references a value the list does not hold
      }
      [ Clear the refusal ] | [ Back to the terms ]
      <i>result.success = false carries no field-level record.</i>
    }
  }
}

@enduml
